WEBVTT

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:07.000
Two tones. One sound in each ear. A beat appears between them. The percept is real.

00:00:07.000 --> 00:00:14.000
The phantom beat. Different frequencies can produce a rhythmic impression. Perception is not a diagnosis.

00:00:14.000 --> 00:00:20.000
1973: Gerald Oster described an auditory phenomenon as a scientific probe, not a wellness trial.

00:00:20.000 --> 00:00:27.000
Does the brain follow? Hearing a rhythm does not prove global EEG entrainment. That is a separate hypothesis.

00:00:27.000 --> 00:00:34.000
2023 systematic review of fourteen EEG studies: five supporting entrainment, eight not, one mixed. Methods varied.

00:00:34.000 --> 00:00:40.000
Ask for the test: what was measured? Was the named audio tested? A promise is not a finding.
